                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2717b459-3959-3c93-a45d-129fa472d360",
                        "entry_id": "b631bddc-309c-32e1-ad10-7a853f46ca57",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Utterly or thoroughly."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6b41e663-ee0f-403a-bab6-66eba1fd5173",
                                "sense_id": "2717b459-3959-3c93-a45d-129fa472d360",
                                "text": "Mr. Cooke at once began a tirade against the residents of Asquith for permitting a sandy and generally disgraceful condition of the roads. So roundly did he vituperate the inn management in particular, and with such a loud flow of words, that I trembled lest he should be heard on the veranda."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "661bb638-60e3-4590-8f19-d62c39289dbf",
                                "sense_id": "2717b459-3959-3c93-a45d-129fa472d360",
                                "text": "When, over in the east, General Valentine Baker led his force of four thousand irregulars against Osman Digna, he was roundly thrashed."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cd9969f6-9696-445b-a892-ce0a5ec60ca5",
                                "sense_id": "2717b459-3959-3c93-a45d-129fa472d360",
                                "text": "A few short years ago, Musk was roundly mocked as a crazy con artist on the verge of going broke. Now this shy South African with Asperger’s syndrome, who escaped a brutal childhood and overcame personal tragedy, bends governments and industry to the force of his ambition."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "da16e64f-5fdd-453a-91f1-3730f428fb4b",
                                "sense_id": "2717b459-3959-3c93-a45d-129fa472d360",
                                "text": "Weak management and a small team of civil servants who were out of their depth have been roundly blamed for the £4 billion overspend on London's Elizabeth line (Crossrail) and its opening four years late in May 2022."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "01006471-8b07-3ec6-8959-0f56cdca9120",
                        "entry_id": "b631bddc-309c-32e1-ad10-7a853f46ca57",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Boldly; openly."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a6baac5a-0fb6-4574-9ae2-c6b5db649eaa",
                                "sense_id": "01006471-8b07-3ec6-8959-0f56cdca9120",
                                "text": "Moko, a name given by sportsmen to pheasants killed by mistake during September, before the pheasant-shooting comes in. They pull out their tails, and roundly assert that they are no pheasants at all, but mokos."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9a9098a4-e72a-33d4-a084-677f3f1d9910",
                        "entry_id": "b631bddc-309c-32e1-ad10-7a853f46ca57",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Briskly."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c701b47e-6603-3b70-8c2a-4288f96a19bd",
                        "entry_id": "b631bddc-309c-32e1-ad10-7a853f46ca57",
